<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Portfolio Page</title>

    <!-- Styleshhet -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/nav.css">

    <!-- Portfolio stylesheet -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/portfolio.css">
</head>
<body>

    <%- include('partials/navbar') %>

    <main class="portfolio-container">
        <section class="portfolio-hero">
            <h1>My Portfolio</h1>
            <p>
                This page highlights my SDEV 305 & SDEV 301 projects and the technologies I used
                to build them.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="portfolio-section">
            <h2>SDEV 305 Projects</h2>

            <article class="project-card">
                <h3>Contact Form Application</h3>

                <p>
                    <strong>Technologies used:</strong>
                    HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Node.js, Express, EJS, and MySQL.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>My role:</strong>
                    I designed the user interface, created the form structure,
                    handled form submission on the server side, and connected the
                    project to the database to save user information.
                </p>

                <div class="project-image-box">
                    <img src="/images/contact.png"
                         alt="Screenshot of the Contact Form application showing form fields and page layout">
                </div>

                <p class="project-links">
                    <strong>GitHub Repo: </strong> <a href="https://github.com/Kiyum06/contact-form" target="_blank">
                        https://github.com/Kiyum06/contact-form</a>
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="project-card">
                <h3>Game Log Application</h3>

                <p>
                    <strong>Technologies used:</strong>
                    HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Node.js, Express, EJS, and MySQL.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>My role:</strong>
                    I worked on styling some part of the web pages, setting up some routes and contribute for 
                    designing the navigation bar.
                </p>

                <div class="project-image-box">
                    <img src="/images/gamelog.png"
                         alt="Screenshot of the Game Log project add-game page and navigation">
                </div>

                <p class="project-links">
                    <strong>GitHub Repo: </strong> <a href="https://github.com/DennysSaenz123/game-log" target="_blank">
                        https://github.com/DennysSaenz123/game-log</a>
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <!-- SDEV 301 section -->
        <section class="portfolio-section">
            <h2>SDEV 301 Projects</h2>

            <article class="project-card">
                <h3>Collectathon: Collaborative GBA Game Project</h3>

                <p>
                    <strong>Technologies used:</strong>
                    C++, Git, GitHub, Butano, mGBA emulator, GitHub Pages,
                    VS Code, and Dev Containers.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>My role:</strong>
                    I worked with a partner to develop and improve a game project
                    while practicing collaborative Git and GitHub workflows. I helped
                    make gameplay changes, resolve merge conflicts, test the game,
                    and update project files such as the README and planning notes.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Key contributions:</strong>
                    I helped modify the player speed, change the background color,
                    update the starting positions of the player and treasure, add
                    a restart feature using the Start button, implement screen looping,
                    and create a limited speed boost feature. I also participated in
                    brainstorming, playtesting, polishing, and preparing the project
                    for GitHub Pages.
                </p>

                <div class="project-image-box">
                    <img src="/images/collectathon.png"
                         alt="Screenshot of the Collectathon game running in the emulator with the player collecting items">
                </div>

                <p class="project-links">
                    <strong>Github Repo: </strong><a href="https://github.com/Kiyum06/collectathon" target="_blank">
                        https://github.com/Kiyum06/collectathon</a>
                </p>
                <p class="project-links">
                    <strong>Live Demo: </strong><a href="https://kiyum06.github.io/collectathon/" target="_blank">
                        https://kiyum06.github.io/collectathon/</a>
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
    </main>

</body>
</html>